Package: vram-fallback-layer
Architecture: amd64 i386
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libc6, libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libvulkan1
Description: Vulkan layer that puts allocations in system RAM when VRAM is full
 When a device-local Vulkan allocation fails because VRAM is full, this
 implicit layer retries it in GPU-accessible system memory instead of
 returning VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY, so games slow down instead of
 crashing.
 .
 The layer is installed as an implicit layer but stays off until a program
 is started with VRAM_FALLBACK=1.
 .
 Install the i386 build of this package as well for 32-bit games.
